.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Container for polygonal data implemented on the basis of NCSA (Urbana, Champagne, Illinois, USA) \fBVSet\fP that forms part of their HDF data file storage\&. 


.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
Stephan Matthai 

.PP
Stephen G\&. Roberts 
.RE
.PP
\fBDate\fP
.RS 4
1996
.RE
.PP
.SH "Motivation"
.PP
Mesh connectivity usually termed as \fBVData\fP typically consists of lists of (1) node and constraint-point coordinates (constraint points can be nodes between nodes but also integration points), (2) a listing of the nodes which belong to each element, and (3) a list of the neighbors of each element\&. If the element lies on the model boundary and there is no neighbor then entries in this list will be UNSPECIFIED\&. (4) A typical \fBVData\fP set also specifies which nodes lie at the model boundary and which property values apply to these nodes\&.

.PP
The class \fBVData\fP brings all these datasets together into an object which holds the information to build this V-type mesh connectivity\&.
.SH "Applicability"
.PP
\fBVData\fP can be used as isolated object but it is also integrated into the \fBVSet\fP which also holds property data which are assigned to the mesh\&.
.SH "Structure"
.PP
The \fBVData\fP object contains coordinate objects, deques of vectors to store the connectivity and maps to hold the boundary flags and boundary values\&.

.PP
Detailed content:

.PP
(double) px, py, pz[0\&.\&.n-1] = coordinates of n nodes (= FE vertices)

.PP
(int8_t) bflags[0\&.\&.n-1] = negative numbers for nodes at boundary, see later

.PP
(enum int8_t) pelmt[0\&.\&.e-1] = \fBCSMP_FEM_TYPE\fP of e finite elements (1 entry only for single element-type mesh)

.PP
(size_t) plist[0\&.\&.e *[sum npe[e]]] = nodes making up each element

.PP
(int64_t) pfverts[0\&.\&.e *[sum fpe[e]]] = neighbor elements adjacent to the faces of each element

.PP
For \fBFace\fP and \fBInterFace\fP objects, 'pfverts' also contains the indices of the higher-dimensional neighbor element\&. 
